DTSTART:20261017T144500Z
DTEND:20261017T164500Z
SUMMARY:The Social Reckoning
LOCATION:Beacon Cinema\, 57 North St\, Pittsfield\, MA 01201
DESCRIPTION:Times: 10:45am\, 1:10pm\, 3:35pm\, 6pm\nInspired by true events
  and the whistleblower who started thesocialmedia reckoningwe’re seeing 
 play out today\, this Aaron Sorkin original screenplay is acompanion piece
  to the hit filmThe Social Networkanda true David and Goliath story. Franc
 esHaugen (Madison)\, a young Facebook engineer\, enlists the help ofJeff H
 orwitz (White)\, a Wall Street Journal reporter\, to go on a dangerous jou
 rney that ends up blowing the whistle on the social network’s most guard
 ed secrets.\nhttps://www.phoenixmovies.net/movies/the-social-reckoning/HO0
 0001772\nFrom Pushpin Western Mass: https://pushpin.city/westernma/
URL:https://www.phoenixmovies.net/movies/the-social-reckoning/HO00001772
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:66055f2f6cc29eaeb6f011a8666d14dcc1f1bfe2@pushpin.city
DTSTAMP:20261017T154538Z
DTSTART:20261017T170000Z
DTEND:20261017T190000Z
SUMMARY:The Metropolitan Opera: Macbeth (2026)
LOCATION:Beacon Cinema\, 57 North St\, Pittsfield\, MA 01201
DESCRIPTION:Two of opera’s most extraordinary artists return to The Met: 
 Live in HD for Verdi’s thrilling take on the immortal Shakespearean tale
  of the scheming couple determined to seize power at any cost. Baritone Qu
 inn Kelsey is the Scottish king haunted by the ghosts of his murderous asc
 ent to the throne\, opposite soprano Lise Davidsen as the power-mad Lady M
 acbeth\, whose ruinous ambition damns them both. Met Music Director Yannic
 k Nézet-Séguin takes the podium for a penetrating production by Louisa P
 roske. Rounding out the all-star cast are tenor Freddie De Tommaso as Macd
 uff and bass-baritone Ryan Speedo Green as Banquo.\nhttps://www.phoenixmov
 ies.net/movies/the-metropolitan-opera:-macbeth-(2026)/HO00001735\nFrom Pus
 hpin Western Mass: https://pushpin.city/westernma/
URL:https://www.phoenixmovies.net/movies/the-metropolitan-opera:-macbeth-(2
 026)/HO00001735
END:VEVENT
